      { title: "Conservation of Energy", emoji: "♾️", content: "The law of conservation of energy states that energy cannot be created or destroyed — only transferred or transformed. The total amount of energy in the universe stays the same. When a ball rolls to a stop, its kinetic energy is not destroyed — it transforms into thermal energy (friction heats the ground slightly) and sound energy. When you turn off a light, the electrical energy stops flowing, but the light and heat energy that were produced dispersed into the environment." }
